Hermes Portable: do not create the default userData folder in the real profile.

applyDesktopIdentity() pins userData for nonstable builds (commit builds are:
appNamePascal "HermesCommit<sha7>") and creates %APPDATA%\<appNamePascal>
before main.ts applies HERMES_DESKTOP_USER_DATA_DIR. Electron resolves
appData through the Windows known-folder API, not the APPDATA variable, so
every portable desktop start left an empty folder in the user's real roaming
profile. Skip the mkdir when the override is set; the override path is
created by main.ts.

diff --git a/apps/desktop/electron/product-identity.ts b/apps/desktop/electron/product-identity.ts
index 8ca5f6cf..6cef9c94 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/electron/product-identity.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/electron/product-identity.ts
@@ -40,7 +40,11 @@ export function applyDesktopIdentity(
   }
 
   const userData: string = path.join(app.getPath('appData'), identity.appNamePascal)
-  mkdirSync(userData, { recursive: true })
+  // Hermes Portable: HERMES_DESKTOP_USER_DATA_DIR replaces this path right after
+  // (main.ts); appData is the real roaming profile, so do not create it there.
+  if (!process.env.HERMES_DESKTOP_USER_DATA_DIR) {
+    mkdirSync(userData, { recursive: true })
+  }
   app.setPath('userData', userData)
   app.setName(identity.displayName)
 
